From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: tell the bundled zlib that unistd.h exists

The build stopped at 17% and took everything downstream with it:

    deps/Dependencies/zlib/gzlib.c:245: error: call to undeclared function 'lseek'
    ... and read, write and close, ten in all, across gzlib.c gzread.c gzwrite.c

gzclose_r and gzclose_w live in gzread.c and gzwrite.c, so the link then reported exactly two
undefined symbols and nothing about the cause.

Play! does not use upstream zlib's CMakeLists - it has its own minimal one in
deps/Dependencies/build_cmake/zlib that compiles the sources directly. Upstream's decides
Z_HAVE_UNISTD_H from a check_include_file() and writes it into a generated zconf.h; this one
generates no zconf.h and never defines the macro, so gzguts.h skips its <unistd.h> and the three
gz* files compile with those four functions undeclared. Under C99 that is an error.

It is latent everywhere and only fires on a libc that does not leak the declarations in through
another header - glibc does, musl does not. Measured on this platform before defining it:
unistd.h is present and lseek links.

diff --git a/deps/Dependencies/build_cmake/zlib/CMakeLists.txt b/deps/Dependencies/build_cmake/zlib/CMakeLists.txt
index 47b7cc7..c67bbd9 100644
--- a/deps/Dependencies/build_cmake/zlib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/deps/Dependencies/build_cmake/zlib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -21,5 +21,11 @@ set(zlib_srcs
 add_library(zlibstatic ${zlib_srcs})
 add_library(ZLIB::ZLIB ALIAS zlibstatic)
 target_compile_definitions(zlibstatic PRIVATE -DLIT_MEM=1)
+# zlib reaches lseek/read/write/close from gzlib.c, gzread.c and gzwrite.c, and gzguts.h includes
+# <unistd.h> for them only under Z_HAVE_UNISTD_H. Upstream zlib's own CMakeLists sets that from a
+# check_include_file() and a generated zconf.h; this minimal build compiles the sources directly
+# and generates neither, so the macro is never defined and those three files compile with the
+# functions undeclared - an error rather than a warning under C99.
+target_compile_definitions(zlibstatic PRIVATE -DZ_HAVE_UNISTD_H=1)
 target_include_directories(zlibstatic PUBLIC ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../../zlib/)
 
